  <ym-title|Weighted field decay from the priced
  mission><label|weighted-field-decay-from-the-priced-mission>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, trace selected-scale producer.

    <item>Status: draft; local review requested, no whole-proof approval.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-small-means.tex>.

    <item>Scope: reorganization of the exact local argument behind the
    weighted field-image estimate <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.small_means>;
    the mission price and chart receipts remain explicit inputs.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact Lean declarations and
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence and status>>>|<row|<cell|Exact
  medium/core identity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.medium>,
  <verbatim|.coreF>, <verbatim|.canal>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|medium>
  is <verbatim|Z.\<beta\>(Stern V i)\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\> Shine5(Z,X)
  \<minus\> Shine5(Z,L.Z)>; <verbatim|canal> rewrites its coordinates as
  <verbatim|Z.\<beta\>(Stern V i)\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\> swale(coreF)>. This
  Arch scale is distinct from <verbatim|\<beta\>\<#302\>(Stern V i)>, the
  weight used in <verbatim|small_means>.>>|<row|<cell|Normalized response and
  night scaling>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Spun>, <verbatim|.fisc>,
  <verbatim|.gazes>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Prism.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.crown>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Path.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Spun.starts>
  writes the response section through inverse chart and the scale-dependent
  evaluation <verbatim|Vault(S,Z,5,k_i,c_i)>. <verbatim|fisc> gives
  <verbatim|Vault(swale x)=crown\<centerdot\>S.project_5(x)> for <verbatim|x>
  odd under the central signed inversion, meaning
  <verbatim|F(archV)x=\<minus\>x> (source predicate <verbatim|Knob.night>).
  The raw grade-five labels map to <verbatim|S_5> under
  <verbatim|P_5=S.project_5>. The manuscript combines these identities with
  <verbatim|crown=\<zeta\>\<centerdot\>(a b)^5> and <verbatim|X.r=a b>; this
  yields <verbatim|z^p b^5 a^5 P_5x>. The frame estimate
  <verbatim|b\<leq\>m=tilt_cap> is <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tiltP>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Cabin.lean>, applied to the
  selected vane's high-scale field.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform local
  price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.ear_price>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/PriceLimit.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ear_price>
  bounds, for each fixed grade-four <verbatim|w> (with a tail that may depend
  on <verbatim|w>), the paired insertion of <verbatim|a^5 P_5(x_i(0))>
  against <verbatim|X.U_i4 w> at the scale-centered point by
  <verbatim|Tau(j,-100)>. Its proof consumes <verbatim|Mission.finances>, the
  finite-volume <verbatim|mileage> price receipt, local cover/core receipts,
  and table projection.>>|<row|<cell|Finite
  detector>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.listened_G>, same
  <verbatim|PriceLimit.lean>; helper <verbatim|YM.Trace.StressFlux.ears_det>
  and <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.sewn> in its immediate imports>|<cell|The
  full family of grade-four front-read pairings separates
  <verbatim|TableOne>. Finite-dimensionality selects a finite family; the
  scale-dependent charts and beacon point give operator-norm convergence, so
  its least singular value remains positive. The manuscript states and proves
  this elementary finite-dimensional implication.>>|<row|<cell|Negative-ticket
  rate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.whither>, <verbatim|.Ticket.prod>,
  <verbatim|.stickK>, <verbatim|.titles>, <verbatim|.ticket_exp>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Fund.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.grow_big>, <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tilt_cap>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/SkyEar.lean>,
  <verbatim|Fund.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|stickK> and <verbatim|titles> provide
  rate-zero tickets for <verbatim|\<beta\>\<#302\>(summit)> and
  <verbatim|tilt_cap>; <verbatim|ticket_exp> gives the rate
  <verbatim|\<minus\>100 Dust> ticket for <verbatim|Tau(-100)>, with
  <verbatim|Dust=1/10000>. <verbatim|Ticket.prod> gives the product rate
  <verbatim|\<minus\>100 Dust\<less\>0>, and <verbatim|whither> proves
  convergence to zero. <verbatim|Gondola.growth>, terminal/stage inequalities
  compare the selected scale <verbatim|z_i> to the summit rate. The
  manuscript writes this product argument; the exact source inequalities are
  the stated inputs.>>|<row|<cell|Final theorem>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.small_means>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Terrain.lean>; applied in
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.hullage>/<verbatim|.legacy>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Garnet.lean>>|<cell|The manuscript
  proves the central tested-coordinate-to-field-norm argument from exact
  scale algebra, the price bound, rate decay, and detector lower bound. It
  does not claim to prove the local price/mileage or selected chart
  receipts.>>>>>

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Read-only inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/{Garnet,Phantom,Limit,Pony}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Terrain,PriceLimit,Prism,Path,Fund,SkyEar,Ears,Cabin}.lean>,
  and <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/{Token,Dray}.lean>. No Lean
  source was changed. No LaTeX or Lean build was run. Blueprint checking is
  recorded with the parent unit record; this new evidence file has not
  independently been run through the checker yet.

